## Clear vs. continue

Each request re-sends the whole context. Clearing costs a one-time rebuild (keynotes ≈ 1.5K plus recently used files) and saves cache reads on every later request. The table lists, per session segment (between compactions), the **first** request where clearing would have paid for itself within 4 requests, and what one clear there would have saved by the end of that segment. It is an upper bound: it ignores whether that moment was a good task boundary.

| Session | At request | Context | Fresh start | Pays off in | Requests after | Saving (ITE) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Synthetic session | #13 of 49 | 88.0K | 33.5K | 1.7 req | 30 | 154K |


